  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between (2S)-2-Hydroxy-N-hydroxybenzylanabasine and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, as this compound is identified as a target of multiple entities that ultimately interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. Specifically, the compound is linked to Integrin beta-6, which is a target of both Lonijaposide T and methyl (2R,4S)-2-(1H-pyrrol-2-yl)-1,3-oxazinane-4-carboxylate, all of which have been shown to target the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The scores for these relationships are consistent, indicating a plausible biological pathway. The mechanism appears to involve the compound acting as a modulator or inhibitor of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through interaction with Integrin beta-6, which may serve as a downstream target. The evidence is robust and consistent across multiple pathways, suggesting a possible role in the regulation of gene expression via the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. However, the exact nature of the interaction and the functional significance of Integrin beta-6 in this context remain areas for further investigation.",
